{"title":"Career Roadmap · Pain Clinic Technician","role":"Pain Clinic Technician","summary":"A Pain Clinic Technician supports multidisciplinary pain-management services under the direction of qualified physicians and other healthcare professionals.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Anaesthesia Assistant / Perfusion / Cardiac Anaesthesia Tech"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Pain Clinic Technician supports multidisciplinary pain-management services under the direction of qualified physicians and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"Pain clinics may manage patients with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chronic back and neck pain"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal pain"},{"text":"Neuropathic pain"},{"text":"Arthritis-related pain"},{"text":"Post-surgical pain"},{"text":"Cancer-related pain"},{"text":"Headache-related conditions"},{"text":"Persistent post-injury pain"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician's role can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Vital-sign monitoring"},{"text":"Treatment-room preparation"},{"text":"Equipment setup"},{"text":"Procedure assistance"},{"text":"Sterile-field support"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Recovery monitoring"},{"text":"Equipment cleaning"},{"text":"Stock management"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“Pain Clinic Technician” is not a single universally standardized clinical qualification. Responsibilities vary by institution. Students should obtain a recognized allied-health/anesthesia-related qualification with appropriate clinical training, and work only within the scope permitted by their qualification and employer. Diagnosis, prescribing and invasive pain procedures remain the responsibility of appropriately qualified clinicians."}]},