"type":"h","text":"Other assessment approaches"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visual Analog Scale"},{"text":"Verbal Rating Scale"},{"text":"Faces-based scales for appropriate patients"},{"text":"Functional pain assessment"},{"text":"Pain should not be assessed only by intensity."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also observe:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Location"},{"text":"Duration"},{"text":"Character"},{"text":"Aggravating factors"},{"text":"Relieving factors"},{"text":"Functional impact"}]}]},{"heading":"Pain Classification","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Nociceptive pain"},{"type":"p","text":"Associated with tissue injury/inflammation."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Musculoskeletal pain"},{"text":"Arthritis"},{"text":"Post-operative pain"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neuropathic pain"},{"type":"p","text":"Associated with nerve injury/dysfunction."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diabetic neuropathy"},{"text":"Radicular pain"},{"text":"Post-herpetic neuralgia"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Nociplastic pain"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Associated with altered pain processing without clear ongoing tissue or nerve injury explaining the pain."},{"text":"Understanding these concepts helps the technician communicate effectively with the clinical team."}]}]},{"heading":"Patient Monitoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Pain procedures can involve sedation, injections or other interventions, so monitoring is important."},{"type":"h","text":"Common parameters"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"Heart rate"},{"text":"Respiratory rate"},{"text":"SpO₂"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Level of consciousness"},{"text":"Pain score"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Baseline Vitals","Procedure Monitoring","Post-Procedure Monitoring","Abnormal Finding?"]},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"↙ ↘"},{"text":"No Yes"},{"text":"↓ ↓"},{"text":"Continue Escalate"},{"text":"Monitoring Immediately"}]}]},{"heading":"Anaesthesia & Sedation Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Because the specialization includes anaesthesia technology, the student should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sedation levels"},{"text":"Airway risks"},{"text":"Oxygen therapy"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Anaesthetic equipment"},{"text":"Emergency airway equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"The Pain Clinic Technician should be able to recognize deterioration and activate emergency support, but should not independently administer anaesthesia or sedation outside their authorized scope."}]},{"heading":"Procedure-Room Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Before procedure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Verify patient identity"},{"text":"Confirm procedure"},{"text":"Prepare equipment"},{"text":"Check monitoring devices"},{"text":"Prepare sterile supplies"},{"text":"Check emergency equipment"},{"text":"Assist with positioning"},{"text":"Confirm documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During procedure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maintain sterile workflow"},{"text":"Assist clinician"},{"text":"Monitor patient"},{"text":"Handle equipment"},{"text":"Document required information"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After procedure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Monitor recovery"},{"text":"Clean equipment"},{"text":"Restock supplies"},{"text":"Document"},{"text":"Support discharge workflow"}]}]},{"heading":"Ultrasound-Guided Pain Procedures","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern pain medicine increasingly uses ultrasound guidance for certain procedures."},{"type":"p","text":"A technician should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic ultrasound terminology"},{"text":"Probe types"},{"text":"Sterile probe-cover technique"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Equipment preparation"},{"text":"Image-display workflow"},{"text":"Needle-procedure support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Positioning","Ultrasound Setup","Sterile Preparation","Clinician Imaging","Procedure","Monitoring","Recovery"]},{"type":"p","text":"The clinician performs the ultrasound-guided procedure."}]},{"heading":"Fluoroscopy & Radiation Safety","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Some interventional pain procedures use fluoroscopy."},{"type":"h","text":"Technician awareness"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation hazards"},{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Personal protective equipment"},{"text":"Dosimetry"},{"text":"Safe positioning"},{"text":"Equipment setup"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core principle"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Minimize Time"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Maximize Distance"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Use Appropriate Shielding"},{"text":"="},{"text":"Radiation Safety"}]}]},{"heading":"Infection Prevention","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Pain procedures may involve invasive techniques, making infection prevention critical."},{"type":"h","text":"Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hand hygiene"},{"text":"Sterile technique"},{"text":"PPE"},{"text":"Skin preparation"},{"text":"Sterile equipment handling"},{"text":"Sharps safety"},{"text":"Biomedical-waste management"},{"text":"Environmental cleaning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Procedure-room workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Clean Environment","Sterile Equipment","Patient Preparation","Procedure","Sharps Disposal","Equipment Decontamination"]}]},{"heading":"Emergency Preparedness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Pain clinics should be prepared for unexpected complications."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible emergencies include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Allergic reactions"},{"text":"Vasovagal episodes"},{"text":"Hypotension"},{"text":"Respiratory depression"},{"text":"Local anaesthetic toxicity"},{"text":"Bleeding"},{"text":"