e-Unit Supervisor"]},{"type":"flow","items":["For maximum employability, combine patient monitoring","anaesthesia fundamentals","pain science","procedure-room assistance","sterile technique","emergency response","equipment management","clinical documentation."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"“Pain Clinic Technician” is best treated as an institution-specific allied-health support role, not as an independently licensed pain practitioner. The technician supports qualified physicians/anesthesiologists/pain specialists with preparation, monitoring, equipment and procedure workflows. Invasive procedures, diagnosis, medication prescribing and definitive treatment decisions remain within the scope of the appropriately qualified clinical professional."}]}]}